you know what you wanna say
and I'm like, don't know,

00:09:57.684 --> 00:10:00.231
and I hadn't even thought
about it, but I'm here for it

00:10:00.231 --> 00:10:02.129
and I'm glad to be speaking.

00:10:02.129 --> 00:10:04.377
But not knowing what I'm trying to convey.

00:10:04.377 --> 00:10:05.887
Hey, that's a great one, two punch, man.

00:10:05.887 --> 00:10:08.332
So yeah. So one, two punch.

00:10:08.332 --> 00:10:09.265
I didn't really know what

00:10:09.265 --> 00:10:10.501
I was gonna say until right before.

00:10:10.501 --> 00:10:12.505
Don't say that. That makes me feel worse.

00:10:12.505 --> 00:10:13.338
But-

00:10:13.338 --> 00:10:14.584
But you did think about it at some point.

00:10:14.584 --> 00:10:15.417
I thought about it.

00:10:15.417 --> 00:10:17.353
Like it was, I thought about it in points.

00:10:17.353 --> 00:10:18.938
It was like, I have three points.

00:10:18.938 --> 00:10:19.953
Do you remember the points?

00:10:19.953 --> 00:10:21.987
No.
Anyway, I mean, come on.

00:10:21.987 --> 00:10:24.590
They would, they'd love
to hear your speech.

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.058
Like paraphrased.

00:10:26.058 --> 00:10:26.926
Wow. Okay.

00:10:26.926 --> 00:10:27.759
Jenna, you might have to help

00:10:27.759 --> 00:10:29.284
with this if it was without memorable.

00:10:29.284 --> 00:10:31.026
You think Jenna remembers your speech?

00:10:31.026 --> 00:10:34.446
Yeah. She was too many libations.

00:10:34.446 --> 00:10:36.280
Don't throw Jenna under the bus.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.887
It was early in the evening.
We were all with it.

00:10:38.887 --> 00:10:41.894
I think I said something like,

00:10:41.894 --> 00:10:44.638
it's great to be back together

00:10:44.638 --> 00:10:48.366
to see the bottom half of your faces.

00:10:48.366 --> 00:10:49.852
Yeah.

00:10:49.852 --> 00:10:52.086
That community is such a big part

00:10:52.086 --> 00:10:54.944
of what we have built here,

00:10:54.944 --> 00:10:57.844
and there's something about being together

00:10:57.844 --> 00:11:00.066
and actually being in
the same physical space,

00:11:00.066 --> 00:11:03.017
and I'm just so excited
that we're able to do this.

00:11:03.017 --> 00:11:04.307
It was about-

00:11:04.307 --> 00:11:05.140
Yeah.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.552
I tapped into the community aspect

00:11:06.552 --> 00:11:07.943
of what we were experiencing.

00:11:07.943 --> 00:11:12.943
And I was like, what he said.
You kind of took it all.

00:11:13.273 --> 00:11:14.654
I can't remember what I said.

00:11:14.654 --> 00:11:17.137
I think I said I love all of you.

00:11:17.137 --> 00:11:19.774
There was some kind of joke about,

00:11:19.774 --> 00:11:22.113
I put my hand on your shoulder.

00:11:22.113 --> 00:11:24.691
And I said, I was like,
you know, sometimes,

00:11:24.691 --> 00:11:25.908
and I put my hand on your shoulder

00:11:25.908 --> 00:11:29.286
like sometimes if you
come into our office,

00:11:29.286 --> 00:11:32.591
this, we do this when
we are like, it was a,

00:11:32.591 --> 00:11:34.033
there was an impromptu moment

00:11:34.033 --> 00:11:36.450
where there was something
about there was a joke.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:39.259
There was a joke about
when we're struggling

00:11:39.259 --> 00:11:40.634
and we're depending on each other.

00:11:40.634 --> 00:11:43.372
And we might come into our
office and we're doing this.

00:11:43.372 --> 00:11:45.111
And then like you turned and we did that.

00:11:45.111 --> 00:11:46.647
We did like a physical joke.

00:11:46.647 --> 00:11:47.480
Yeah.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:50.209
And then I made an HR joke,
which I hate making HR jokes.

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:51.952
We always tend to make a-

00:11:51.952 --> 00:11:53.665
But Ellen was there.

00:11:53.665 --> 00:11:55.031
And so I was just like,

00:11:55.031 --> 00:11:57.121
if you are gonna touch
someone on the shoulders,

00:11:57.121 --> 00:12:00.272
check with Ellen first or
something like that, you know.

00:12:00.272 --> 00:12:01.713
I don't like to make those jokes.

00:12:01.713 --> 00:12:03.919
And I wouldn't have made
that joke if I had really,

00:12:03.919 --> 00:12:05.870
see, this is why I plan things.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.354
Because when you don't plan things,

00:12:07.354 --> 00:12:08.860
you end up making that
joke and everybody laughed

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:11.554
and everybody knew it
was, you know, harmless,

00:12:11.554 --> 00:12:13.271
and we're talking about shoulder touching.

00:12:13.271 --> 00:12:14.674
And I made the one thing

00:12:14.674 --> 00:12:18.262
I do remember saying was the phrase,

00:12:18.262 --> 00:12:20.899
now we're gonna kick
this party up a notch.

00:12:20.899 --> 00:12:22.006
So-
I don't know what,

00:12:22.006 --> 00:12:24.356
remember I said something
like that and I don't know-

00:12:24.356 --> 00:12:25.670
You were feeling it.
I don't know.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:26.918
This is a natural DJ instinct.

00:12:26.918 --> 00:12:27.839
Yeah, I don't know why I said

00:12:27.839 --> 00:12:29.858
that because I wasn't thinking.

00:12:29.858 --> 00:12:30.691
I was-

00:12:30.691 --> 00:12:31.524
You were like, I'm not
prepared to kick it up a notch.

00:12:31.524 --> 00:12:33.110
No, I was thinking I had a playlist

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:35.886
that was gonna take it up like one notch.

00:12:35.886 --> 00:12:36.850
Okay. So what-

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:37.809
So then I started,

00:12:37.809 --> 00:12:39.529
but then I wasn't ready to play it yet

00:12:39.529 --> 00:12:41.972
because there were a few more
songs in my existing playlist.

00:12:41.972 --> 00:12:44.766
Well, give me an example of
what the middle playlist was,

00:12:44.766 --> 00:12:46.091
the taking it up at one notch.

00:12:46.091 --> 00:12:48.343
Well, it had lyrics.

00:12:48.343 --> 00:12:49.176
Okay.

00:12:49.176 --> 00:12:51.059
So it was some-
It had lyrics.

00:12:51.059 --> 00:12:55.976
It was some late '90s rap,
which I thought would connect.

00:12:57.116 --> 00:13:00.366
Like Ice Cube's "Today Was A Good Day".

00:13:02.096 --> 00:13:03.840
But still kinda like.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:04.681
Yeah, still vibing.

00:13:04.681 --> 00:13:06.413
We're all interacting with each other.

00:13:06.413 --> 00:13:08.039
And, but I didn't change the playlist yet.

00:13:08.039 --> 00:13:09.198
And I went back and sat down,

00:13:09.198 --> 00:13:12.744
and Jenna leaned over and she said,

00:13:12.744 --> 00:13:15.812
"Is this your idea of
kicking it up a notch?"

00:13:15.812 --> 00:13:16.645
Jenna!

00:13:18.348 --> 00:13:19.765
And I was like,

00:13:20.646 --> 00:13:22.532
yeah, I don't know why
I said that prematurely

00:13:22.532 --> 00:13:24.494
because I wasn't ready
to kick it up a notch.

00:13:24.494 --> 00:13:25.327
Is this your idea of
kicking it up a notch?

00:13:25.327 --> 00:13:26.160
And I was like, you know what?

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.674
I can do that. I can do that.

00:13:27.674 --> 00:13:31.976
And I went over there and then
like, I started, I actually,

00:13:31.976 --> 00:13:33.734
I think I went to use the bathroom.

00:13:33.734 --> 00:13:35.319
I was like, I gotta compose myself.

00:13:35.319 --> 00:13:36.578
And when I came back out,

00:13:36.578 --> 00:13:38.895
Jenna said, I don't
think, she came up to me.

00:13:38.895 --> 00:13:41.902
And it was like a little, like,

00:13:41.902 --> 00:13:44.332
I'm whispering even though
there's no one around.

00:13:44.332 --> 00:13:45.165
Yeah. Right.

00:13:45.165 --> 00:13:46.748
And she was like,

00:13:47.917 --> 00:13:51.264
"People are coming up to
me because I don't think

00:13:51.264 --> 00:13:53.981
that they're comfortable
coming up to you."

00:13:53.981 --> 00:13:54.814
I love this.

00:13:54.814 --> 00:13:57.071
"And they're just asking,

00:13:57.071 --> 00:14:01.571
could we have music with,
you know, with like lyrics?"

00:14:02.453 --> 00:14:03.704
Okay.

00:14:03.704 --> 00:14:05.278
The music already had a beat.

00:14:05.278 --> 00:14:06.111
Okay.

00:14:06.111 --> 00:14:07.096
And then she was like, you know,

00:14:07.096 --> 00:14:09.047
"I think people want to dance."

00:14:09.047 --> 00:14:12.934
And I was like, people want to dance?

00:14:12.934 --> 00:14:15.028
And I looked around at how everyone

00:14:15.028 --> 00:14:17.262
there was younger than me.

00:14:17.262 --> 00:14:18.175
Well-
And I was like,

00:14:18.175 --> 00:14:19.069
you know what?

00:14:19.069 --> 00:14:19.902
Significantly younger.

00:14:19.902 --> 00:14:22.125
And I'm like, yeah, the
people who work here,

00:14:22.125 --> 00:14:24.409
yeah, they're in a different head space.

00:14:24.409 --> 00:14:25.868
When they want, I was like,

00:14:25.868 --> 00:14:28.159
but they haven't seen
each other for so long.

00:14:28.159 --> 00:14:29.883
So many people have never met.

00:14:29.883 --> 00:14:32.681
Don't they just wanna sit down and talk?

00:14:32.681 --> 00:14:34.645
And Jenna was like, "No."

00:14:34.645 --> 00:14:35.501
We did it already.

00:14:35.501 --> 00:14:37.335
We did it already. We've been doing that.

00:14:37.335 --> 00:14:38.168
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:14:38.168 --> 00:14:40.758
And I'm like, okay, okay.

00:14:40.758 --> 00:14:43.916
Well, then I'm thinking my backup

00:14:43.916 --> 00:14:47.519
to my backup playlist to
take it up a second notch

00:14:47.519 --> 00:14:50.427
is still not taking us to the dance floor.

00:14:50.427 --> 00:14:52.081
You weren't prepared for a dance party.

00:14:52.081 --> 00:14:53.560
I wasn't prepared for a dance party.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:56.292
And that was such a
huge blind spot for me.

00:14:56.292 --> 00:14:58.179
Yeah. Well, every DJ's
gotta have that moment.

00:14:58.179 --> 00:14:59.905
And a big wake up call.

00:14:59.905 --> 00:15:01.231
This is gonna be in your DJ,

00:15:01.231 --> 00:15:04.246
when you write your DJ autobiography,

00:15:04.246 --> 00:15:05.079
this is gonna be called,

00:15:05.079 --> 00:15:07.306
the chapter's gonna be
called wake up call,

00:15:07.306 --> 00:15:08.449
and you're gonna tell this story.

00:15:08.449 --> 00:15:10.713
Yeah, so then I go, you know,

00:15:10.713 --> 00:15:13.679
I read Questlove's book and-

00:15:13.679 --> 00:15:14.562
Did he have a wake up call?

00:15:14.562 --> 00:15:15.822
He had a wake up call.

00:15:15.822 --> 00:15:20.239
He tells this fantastic
story of how President Obama,

00:15:21.554 --> 00:15:24.637
he was sitting president at the time,

00:15:25.832 --> 00:15:28.091
invited him to an event.

00:15:28.091 --> 00:15:31.758
And Questlove had been
working on a set list

00:15:34.466 --> 00:15:38.054
for like months and months
and months leading up to this.

00:15:38.054 --> 00:15:41.729
And it was like, go, it was
like this amazingly intricate,

00:15:41.729 --> 00:15:46.479
like goes from A to B, goes
through the history of music.

00:15:47.321 --> 00:15:51.238
And it's like this amazing,
intricate set list.

00:15:52.732 --> 00:15:54.886
And then he's playing it for Obama.

00:15:54.886 --> 00:15:57.577
This is like, this is
a big moment for him.

00:15:57.577 --> 00:16:01.327
And then after a while,
President Obama pull,

00:16:03.569 --> 00:16:06.210
comes up to him, pulls
him aside and you know,

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:09.670
he does an impression of
him and is basically like,

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:11.889
"Can you play something for the kids?

00:16:11.889 --> 00:16:14.051
Can you play something for the kids?"

00:16:14.051 --> 00:16:15.566
And that's my Obama, by the way.

00:16:15.566 --> 00:16:16.634
That's pretty good.

00:16:16.634 --> 00:16:18.384
And he was crushed.

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:23.774
He started, he had to start
googling on his phone.

00:16:23.774 --> 00:16:26.061
I mean, Questlove, it's
not that he didn't know

00:16:26.061 --> 00:16:28.298
what the kids would want to listen to.

00:16:28.298 --> 00:16:31.064
Who, what kids, the Obama kids?

00:16:31.064 --> 00:16:33.290
The younger people who were there.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:34.123
The kids.

00:16:34.123 --> 00:16:35.407
And then so like,

00:16:35.407 --> 00:16:39.384
can you play some current hits, you know?

00:16:39.384 --> 00:16:43.388
And so he like totally
off the, on the fly,

00:16:43.388 --> 00:16:45.896
just had to regroup entirely.

00:16:45.896 --> 00:16:46.729
Wow.

00:16:46.729 --> 00:16:48.587
And then he had to start playing-

00:16:48.587 --> 00:16:49.420
Wake up call, man.

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:51.877
Had to start playing
what the people wanted

00:16:51.877 --> 00:16:54.975
to hear right then and dance to.

00:16:54.975 --> 00:16:58.066
And then I think there's a part

00:16:58.066 --> 00:17:00.081
of the story where he is like,

00:17:00.081 --> 00:17:03.824
when it was all over, when
the party was over, he just,

00:17:03.824 --> 00:17:06.157
he snuck away and just left.

00:17:07.256 --> 00:17:11.547
And he said that he couldn't
DJ for like the year.

00:17:11.547 --> 00:17:12.380
Oh my.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:16.215
It was like a huge deal for him. And-

00:17:16.215 --> 00:17:17.864
This is a much better story than yours.

00:17:17.864 --> 00:17:21.205
I'm so grateful to hear
his much better story,

00:17:21.205 --> 00:17:23.115
because then I was like, you know what?

00:17:23.115 --> 00:17:25.262
I'm just, I don't even, I'm not a DJ.

00:17:25.262 --> 00:17:26.746
I don't even have DJ equipment.

00:17:26.746 --> 00:17:27.579
Yet.

00:17:27.579 --> 00:17:29.553
I'm sitting here with a, with Spotify.

00:17:29.553 --> 00:17:30.568
Hold on, but you're ready to get,

00:17:30.568 --> 00:17:31.591
you are gonna buy some.

00:17:31.591 --> 00:17:34.194
And then at this point,
I'm like, all right.

00:17:34.194 --> 00:17:37.694
So I start kicking it up with what I know.

00:17:39.228 --> 00:17:41.728
I'm playing some late '90s rap

00:17:43.688 --> 00:17:45.469
and people are going on the dance floor.

00:17:45.469 --> 00:17:47.940
And then I'm like, I'll take requests.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:50.865
And then based on the first few requests,

00:17:50.865 --> 00:17:53.996
I mean, these are songs that I knew of.

00:17:53.996 --> 00:17:55.894
I was aware of them and
I would like find them

00:17:55.894 --> 00:17:57.211
and put 'em in the queue.

00:17:57.211 --> 00:17:59.740
And then I was like, I
hope people don't see this.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:02.124
And then I like took those
songs and I started googling.

00:18:02.124 --> 00:18:06.874
Like, I'm like, these people
like mid-2000's dance floor.

00:18:08.035 --> 00:18:11.082
Hit the dance floor. Like,
I'm literally Googling this.

00:18:11.082 --> 00:18:13.236
And then I'm over there like, yeah, okay.

00:18:13.236 --> 00:18:14.421
And then I'm throwing
songs in the playlist.

00:18:14.421 --> 00:18:16.334
And I'm like, okay, now I got this.

00:18:16.334 --> 00:18:17.696
People are giving requests,

00:18:17.696 --> 00:18:21.243
it's getting dark, everybody's
dancing. And you know what?

00:18:21.243 --> 00:18:23.167
It started to work. It started to work.

00:18:23.167 --> 00:18:24.000
It did.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.314
I, the thing I was observing,

00:18:25.314 --> 00:18:27.341
'cause I was not party to any of this.

00:18:27.341 --> 00:18:29.252
I wasn't talking to,

00:18:29.252 --> 00:18:31.905
I didn't talk to you other
than when we'd give a speech.

00:18:31.905 --> 00:18:32.738
We tend to-

00:18:32.738 --> 00:18:33.571
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:33.571 --> 00:18:34.404
We tend to separate-

00:18:34.404 --> 00:18:35.908
Right.
In glad hand separately.

00:18:35.908 --> 00:18:37.230
Yeah.

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:38.896
We're too-
Divide and conquer.

00:18:38.896 --> 00:18:39.729
We're too accepting
dudes. There's two of us.

00:18:39.729 --> 00:18:42.113
Divide the party.

00:18:42.113 --> 00:18:43.580
But the thing I noticed was

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:48.580
I hadn't seen the Mythical
crew together to that degree.

00:18:48.848 --> 00:18:53.304
And we also had the Smash crew,
you know, in two years and-

00:18:53.304 --> 00:18:54.137
Yeah.

00:18:54.137 --> 00:18:57.115
We've hired a bunch of people
over the past two years

00:18:57.115 --> 00:18:59.960
and you know, we keep getting older

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:03.862
and we keep hiring people who are younger.

00:19:03.862 --> 00:19:06.914
And so there are just a lot of,

00:19:06.914 --> 00:19:10.155
most people are in their 20s
and many of them are like

00:19:10.155 --> 00:19:12.978
in their early and mid 20s, right?

00:19:12.978 --> 00:19:13.811
Yeah.

00:19:13.811 --> 00:19:16.086
And there's just a
different life stage, man.

00:19:16.086 --> 00:19:17.517
And yeah, they wanna dance

00:19:17.517 --> 00:19:19.607
and it was just like, it was amazing.

00:19:19.607 --> 00:19:21.961
Once they started hearing
what they wanted to hear,

00:19:21.961 --> 00:19:24.274
it was like a release and
it, and you know what-

00:19:24.274 --> 00:19:28.107
It was like letting
people out of, you know,

00:19:29.021 --> 00:19:30.900
they would've been like cooped up.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:32.647
Yeah.
Socially.

00:19:32.647 --> 00:19:33.970
And they were just letting loose.

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:35.255
And it was a beautiful thing to watch.

00:19:35.255 --> 00:19:37.002
It did feel good to see

00:19:37.002 --> 00:19:40.318
the Mythical crew and the
Smash crew come together

00:19:40.318 --> 00:19:41.914
and hang out and have a good time,

00:19:41.914 --> 00:19:44.099
and nobody wanted to leave the party.

00:19:44.099 --> 00:19:46.827
They all just wanted to dance
or hang around the edge.

00:19:46.827 --> 00:19:49.495
And it like, the party really took a turn.

00:19:49.495 --> 00:19:51.781
Thank you, Jenna, for breaking the news.

00:19:51.781 --> 00:19:52.770
Yes.
And I was like,

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:54.759
I went up to Christie and I was like,

00:19:54.759 --> 00:19:58.920
"Yeah, this is, I've really
gotta make some adjustments."

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.739
She was like, "You can do it, babe."

00:20:00.739 --> 00:20:02.479
She's like being very supportive.

00:20:02.479 --> 00:20:05.289
And then so then yeah,
the party started jumping.

00:20:05.289 --> 00:20:06.122
Yeah.

00:20:06.122 --> 00:20:08.331
And I was like Googling
and taking requests

00:20:08.331 --> 00:20:09.297
and figuring it out.

00:20:09.297 --> 00:20:10.633
And people were like, looking at me like,

00:20:10.633 --> 00:20:12.723
man, he's just taking
this really seriously.

00:20:12.723 --> 00:20:14.957
Now can I get you, just as you're,

00:20:14.957 --> 00:20:18.077
you know, I believe in
this career evolution.

00:20:18.077 --> 00:20:20.827
I like the idea of your DJ phase.

00:20:23.537 --> 00:20:25.424
You know, we're jokingly
